  "about": "Difficulty 6. The electro lead and the clap set the accents (1, 1.5, 3); the verse doubles end on the 7 / 7.25 kick pickup, the hooks on sixteenth doubles off the lead (1.5 / 1.75, 5.5 / 5.75); builds climb in quarters; four freezes across the two breaks; free-tap bars every beat. Captured-move short names (robot, sidefreeze, moonwalk, and the same two in the final hook) still play their family's library clip, as they always did; the second hook opts in to the CAPTURES by naming their ids (ehBc: dance_toprock_kick, dance_power_helicopter — the same families, beats and accents as ehB, so the steps, the cap and the pay are the same). The last hook ends in a FREESTYLE section (efreeH: the same free taps, marked): the buttons pick the move, MATCH is not asked, and it pays STYLE only. Accents, doubles and free taps are STYLE taps; only the moves are scored steps.",
